What gives?

249
00:14:48,220 --> 00:14:49,917
How'd you destroy my trap card?

250
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:51,360
Ha ha ha ha ha!

251
00:14:51,700 --> 00:14:55,620
Haven't you noticed the monster
I've chosen to be my deck master?

252
00:14:55,880 --> 00:14:56,800
It's Jinzo!

253
00:14:56,980 --> 00:14:59,380
My trap cards are useless! That's right!

254
00:14:59,520 --> 00:15:02,226
He'll automatically
destroy every one of them!

255
00:15:02,520 --> 00:15:03,350
Huh!

256
00:15:03,433 --> 00:15:08,580
Now I play the magic card, Pot of Green,
allowing me to draw two more cards!

257
00:15:11,440 --> 00:15:12,270
Excellent!

258
00:15:12,920 --> 00:15:13,750
Ha!

259
00:15:13,833 --> 00:15:17,297
You just played a magic card which
triggers my Vault Scout special ability!

260
00:15:17,380 --> 00:15:20,260
so it gains 200 attack points.

261
00:15:20,640 --> 00:15:22,080
Now, is that so?

262
00:15:22,320 --> 00:15:28,000
He won't be around for much longer
anyway, for I summon my Fairy Lily.

263
00:15:29,560 --> 00:15:30,390
Ha!

264
00:15:30,840 --> 00:15:34,140
Looks like she's only got
400 attack points, Lecter.

265
00:15:34,480 --> 00:15:36,340
Looks can be deceiving, Joy.

266
00:15:36,580 --> 00:15:40,380
I give up 2,000 life points
to increase her power.

267
00:15:41,360 --> 00:15:43,840
Lily, destroy his Desvolt scout.

268
00:15:49,280 --> 00:15:53,080
That maneuver cost you more
life points than it cost me.

269
00:15:54,200 --> 00:16:00,140
Not exactly, because I'm about to restore
mine with my Sevix Blessing Magic card.

270
00:16:01,420 --> 00:16:03,320
What's the deal with that card?

271
00:16:03,560 --> 00:16:08,980
It increases Lecter's life points by the
same number of life points I just lost.

272
00:16:09,820 --> 00:16:10,650
Exactly!

273
00:16:10,920 --> 00:16:15,160
And if my math is correct, that
gives me 1,000 more life points.

274
00:16:15,960 --> 00:16:18,600
And finally, I'll place
one card face down.

275
00:16:18,900 --> 00:16:24,140
Soon we'll claim four more of your bodies,
leaving your minds trapped here. You!

276
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:26,400
We gotta do something and fast!

277
00:16:28,440 --> 00:16:30,060
Get ready, boys.

278
00:16:30,600 --> 00:16:33,220
To give up your bodies, there it is.

279
00:16:33,480 --> 00:16:35,660
I've just activated Gravity Bind,

280
00:16:35,840 --> 00:16:39,237
which stops all monsters with
four more stars from attacking.

281
00:16:39,320 --> 00:16:42,040
That includes everything
except my fairy lily.

282
00:16:42,280 --> 00:16:43,317
That's a trap!

283
00:16:43,400 --> 00:16:47,420
And your Jinzo's supposed to
destroy all trap cards on the field.

284
00:16:47,540 --> 00:16:50,760
That's usually true, but
since Jinzo's my deckmaster,

285
00:16:51,040 --> 00:16:54,260
he only destroys my
opponent's traps. Aw, yeah?

286
00:16:55,460 --> 00:16:56,600
Now, awesome.

287
00:16:57,020 --> 00:17:00,937
This body-snatching bozo's about
to get a taste of his own medicine,

288
00:17:01,020 --> 00:17:02,720
because I got a Jinzo, too.

289
00:17:03,060 --> 00:17:06,620
I sacrificed Panther Warrior
so I can summon this.

290
00:17:06,860 --> 00:17:08,220
My own Jinzo.

291
00:17:10,520 --> 00:17:14,280
Your Jinzo may not cooperate,
but mine definitely will

292
00:17:15,580 --> 00:17:18,720
All right, Jinzo, destroy his trap

293
00:17:26,380 --> 00:17:27,210
Aw, yeah!

294
00:17:27,293 --> 00:17:29,340
Celebrating so soon? Yeah, why?

295
00:17:29,600 --> 00:17:31,517
You may have destroyed my trap card,

296
00:17:31,600 --> 00:17:35,237
but my fairy lily is still the
strongest monster on the field, Mr.

297
00:17:35,320 --> 00:17:40,640
Wheeler Once I power her up again, she'll
wipe out your Jinzo and your life points.

298
00:17:40,860 --> 00:17:41,690
Eh?

299
00:17:41,773 --> 00:17:43,220
Joey, Lecter is right.

300
00:17:43,580 --> 00:17:46,017
Her special ability allows
him to raise her attack

301
00:17:46,100 --> 00:17:48,677
points higher than any
other monster on the field.

302
00:17:48,760 --> 00:17:49,590
Oh, yeah.

303
00:17:49,860 --> 00:17:53,900
But then again, attack points
aren't everything, are they, Joey?

304
00:17:54,480 --> 00:17:55,400
Wait a sec.

305
00:17:55,700 --> 00:17:57,377
Yuki's trying to tell me something.

306
00:17:57,460 --> 00:18:00,557
There is a way to crush this guy's
monster before it crushes me.

307
00:18:00,640 --> 00:18:03,960
Even though Lecter can raise
his fairy's attack points,

308
00:18:04,260 --> 00:18:06,360
her defense points stay pretty low.

309
00:18:07,380 --> 00:18:09,540
I play Flock Attack!

310
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:13,765
This magic card switches your
fairy from attack to defense mode!

311
00:18:14,460 --> 00:18:15,800
You can't!

312
00:18:16,400 --> 00:18:17,900
I just did!

313
00:18:18,360 --> 00:18:23,066
Jinzo, do us all a favor and send his
little monster back to Fairyland, will ya?

314
00:18:23,560 --> 00:18:25,220
Cyber Energy Shock Attack!

315
00:18:28,540 --> 00:18:31,000
Well, that's all for me, Lecter.

316
00:18:31,600 --> 00:18:33,160
Now, back to you, Yook.

317
00:18:33,440 --> 00:18:34,560
Pound this poser.

318
00:18:35,260 --> 00:18:36,090
Right.

319
00:18:36,173 --> 00:18:37,600
Time to take you down.

320
00:18:39,340 --> 00:18:42,600
And I have just the card
to do it in my head.

321
00:18:43,720 --> 00:18:45,780
Come forth, Dark Magician Girl!

322
00:18:47,540 --> 00:18:49,900
Your light points are wide open!

323
00:18:50,300 --> 00:18:52,680
Dark Magician Girl, attack him directly!

324
00:18:58,960 --> 00:19:01,460
He just lost 2,000 life points.

325
00:19:03,420 --> 00:19:04,700
It's your move.

326
00:19:06,860 --> 00:19:13,560
The time has arrived, my young friends,
to reap the benefits of my magic card.

327
00:19:13,800 --> 00:19:14,720
Say what, man?

328
00:19:15,600 --> 00:19:16,780
Wait, he's right.

329
00:19:17,020 --> 00:19:19,777
It's been three turns since
he played Altar of Mist.

330
00:19:19,860 --> 00:19:22,800
Now he can summon almost
any monster he wants.

331
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:24,160
You are correct.

332
00:19:28,940 --> 00:19:30,980
What's so funny, Lecter?

333
00:19:33,960 --> 00:19:35,880
That's getting real annoying.

334
00:19:37,200 --> 00:19:39,780
If you were me, you'd laugh, too.

335
00:19:40,640 --> 00:19:45,780
For in my hands, I hold the Big
Five's most powerful creature.

336
00:19:46,300 --> 00:19:48,460
Say goodbye to your bodies.

337
00:20:00,100 --> 00:20:02,020
You're mine.

338
00:20:05,760 --> 00:20:07,340
You're mine.

339
00:20:25,220 --> 00:20:25,954
Thank you.
